  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"Whenever $A,$ then $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$A$ whenever $B$\" means $B⇒A$\n\n- \"$B,$ provided that $A$\" means $A⇒B$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\text{Whenever }A\\text{, then }B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A\\text{ whenever }B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $B,\\text{ provided that }A$ | $A⇒B$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
